    <briefdescription>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>Scalar value iterator.</para><para>Scalar value iterators iterate over each scalar value in the set. Two caveats to beware of:</para><para><itemizedlist>
<listitem><para>The set can hold a very large number of values, even the entire value space, in which case iterating over values rather than storage nodes could take a very long time. </para></listitem>
<listitem><para>Iterating over values for a non-integral type is most likely nonsensical. </para></listitem>
</itemizedlist>
</para>    </detaileddescription>
